# MASTER BUILD PROMPT: SyncCode — Real-Time Collaborative Coding & Video Calling Platform

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, software architect, UI/UX designer, security engineer, and QA engineer.

Build a complete, functional, internet-connected web application called **SyncCode**. It is a collaborative coding workspace where 4–6 users can join the same room, write code simultaneously, see live changes, communicate through audio/video calls, share their screens, discuss code in chat, and save project versions.

This is a real software engineering project intended for a Java Full Stack Developer portfolio. Do not build only a landing page, static dashboard, UI mockup, or frontend simulation. Implement the real frontend, Java backend, database persistence, real-time collaboration, calling integration, authentication, error handling, tests, and deployment configuration.

If the environment cannot generate all files in one pass, build the project incrementally and maintain a checklist of completed and remaining features. Never claim a feature works until its implementation and configuration are present.

