# 24. Definition of Done

The project is not complete until all implemented core flows work.

Required core acceptance criteria:
1. A new user can register and log in.
2. User and project data persist in MongoDB.
3. A user can create a private coding room.
4. The owner can invite teammates through a shareable link.
5. Up to 6 active participants can join a room.
6. A seventh participant is rejected with a clear message.
7. Multiple authorized users can edit the same file concurrently.
8. All connected editors converge on the same code.
9. Documents are saved durably and restored after reconnection/restart.
10. Real audio/video calls work when LiveKit is configured.
11. Users can mute/unmute and turn camera on/off.
12. Screen sharing works when supported and authorized.
13. Users can send room chat messages.
14. Users can create and restore snapshots.
15. Permissions prevent viewers from editing and outsiders from accessing private rooms.
16. Theme and editor preferences persist across logins.
17. The frontend, backend, and collaboration service run with documented commands.
